# Unity Coding

## Stack

- **Unity 6.3 LTS**, C#, URP, **Input System**, **uGUI**
- Camera SSOT: **TopDownCamera** — do not treat Cinemachine as camera authority
- Prefer existing project patterns over generic Unity tutorials (Unity 4/old Input Manager style)

## Do

- Cache references; avoid per-frame `Find` / `FindObjectOfType` / string `GameObject.Find`
- Prefer **events** for gameplay signals / cross-system notify; **coroutines OK** for timed sequences / waits
- Prefer injected refs over polling by name
- Keep `Update` lean; move heavy work off hot paths
- Inspector-driven tuning for combat/traps (no hardcoded balance magic without reason)
- Match existing naming and folder layout when adding scripts

## Don't

- Don't swap stack: UI Toolkit, DOTS/ECS, Cinemachine-as-SSOT, old Input Manager (unless user asks)
- Don't assume missing classes or APIs exist — check the repo or ask
- Don't wholesale-replace files when a small edit works
